    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (26 tests, 0 failures/errors).\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed the `customerCode` format from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` with a per-city sequence.\n\n**`AssignCustomerCode.java`** (the one place the code is built) now:\n- Takes `CITY3` = upper-cased first three letters of the owner's city.\n- Keeps `LAST3` = upper-cased first three letters of the last name.\n- Computes `NNNN` as a **per-city** sequence \u2014 one more than the number of existing owners already in that city (counted case-insensitively over `findAll()`, before the new owner is saved so it's excluded), zero-padded to 4 digits.\n\n**Values derived from `customerCode` rebuild automatically:** the `membershipNumber` in `OwnerMapper` is `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, so it now naturally reads e.g. `SYD-ALP-0001-M26` since it's composed from the (new) `customerCode` field rather than re-deriving from name \u2014 no code change needed there, only the doc-comment example updated.\n\nI also updated the doc comments in `AssignCustomerCode.java`, the `owners.POST.yml` step comment, and the `OwnerMapper` example to reflect the new format.\n\nTests confirming the behavior: `Cp16` (format regex `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}`), `Cp09` (same-city consecutive sequence, `SYD-ALP-`/`SYD-BRA-`), and `Cp14` (membership number over the city-prefixed code) all pass, along with the rest of the suite.",
